   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The alphabet",
     "texto": [
      "The Danish alphabet has 29 letters. It uses the same letters as English, plus three of its own at the end: **æ, ø, å**. It has no **ñ**.\n\nIn Danish, **c, q, w, x** and **z** appear mostly in loanwords and foreign names, unlike in English."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Vowels you already know",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Letter",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Sounds like…",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "**a**",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "between the «a» in «father» and the «e» in «bed»; in these examples it comes close to an open «e»",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "kat, gade",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "**e**",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "like the first sound of «day», without the glide",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "en",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "**i**",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "like the «ee» in «see»",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "minut",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "**o**",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "o; the long one is tighter than in English «oh», with no «w» glide",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "hoste",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "**u**",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "like the «oo» in «food»",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "du, drue",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ]
     ],
     "nota": "At the end of a word, the **e** weakens and sounds very faint: gad**e**, læs**e**.",
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "New vowels",
