    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Long or short?",
     "texto": [
      "Length depends on the syllable and can't be predicted without exceptions. As a first clue, the stressed vowel is usually short before a double consonant, and long at the end or before a consonant + vowel:\n\n- Short: ly**kk**e.\n- Long: g**a**de, bl**å**."
     ],
     "tutora": "pensando"
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
